Terminal 1 – Full Port Discovery
nmap -Pn -p- -sT -T4 --min-rate 5000 iapp192644.croydon.ms.com -oA ports

Purpose:

Find all TCP ports
Fastest initial scan
No Npcap required
Terminal 2 – Service Enumeration
nmap -Pn -sT -sV -sC -T4 iapp192644.croydon.ms.com -oA services

Purpose:

Service versions
Default NSE scripts
Banner grabbing
Terminal 3 – Web Enumeration
nmap -Pn -sT \
--script=http-title,http-headers,http-methods,http-enum,http-server-header,http-security-headers,http-robots.txt \
-p80,443,8080,8443 iapp192644.croydon.ms.com -oA web

Purpose:

Headers
Methods
Interesting directories
Security headers
Technology fingerprinting
Terminal 4 – SSL/TLS Assessment
nmap -Pn -sT \
--script=ssl-cert,ssl-enum-ciphers \
-p443,8443 iapp192644.croydon.ms.com -oA ssl

Purpose:

TLS versions
Weak ciphers
Certificate details
Terminal 5 – Vulnerability Scripts
nmap -Pn -sT \
--script=vuln \
-p80,443,8080,8443 iapp192644.croydon.ms.com -oA vuln

Purpose:

Common CVE checks
Misconfigurations
Known service vulnerabilities
Everything in One Command

If you want maximum coverage in one shot:

nmap -Pn -p- -sT -sV -sC -T4 \
--script=vuln,http-title,http-headers,http-methods,http-enum,http-security-headers,http-robots.txt,ssl-cert,ssl-enum-ciphers \
iapp192644.croydon.ms.com -oA fullscan

Note: This may run for several hours because:

All 65535 ports
Version detection
Default scripts
Vulnerability scripts
HTTP enumeration
SSL checks
